Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-multi-select, add-marquee-selection

Goal:
Support `Ctrl+A` / `Cmd+A` in Canvas Mode to select every selectable canvas element at once.

Context:
The user expects standard select-all behavior. Multi-selection already exists, so this task should extend the keyboard path to build a selection containing all selectable canvas items instead of only supporting manual click or marquee accumulation.

Expected changes:

- inspect the canvas keyboard shortcut handling path
- add `Ctrl+A` / `Cmd+A` handling in Canvas Mode
- build a complete selection containing every selectable stroke, shape, text item, image, and imported PDF page
- prevent the browser default “select page text” behavior inside the Tauri webview

Acceptance criteria:

- Pressing `Ctrl+A` / `Cmd+A` in Canvas Mode selects all selectable canvas items.
- The resulting selection works with the existing move, resize, style-edit, and delete-selection flows.
- The browser/webview default text-selection behavior does not interfere.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Keep this Canvas-only unless there is already a parallel selection model in PDF Mode.
- This task should complement, not replace, marquee and manual additive selection.
